Bill of Materials & Wiring Reference

Component list

|  | Component | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Brushless motors, 2212 900–920KV (x4) | Generate thrust for flight |
| 2 | ESC, 40A, 2–6S (x4) | Converts PWM signal to 3-phase power for motors |
| 3 | Wiring | Electrical connections between subsystems |
| 4 | Pixhawk 6C | Flight controller — manages sensors and overall flight |
| 5 | Telemetry, 433 MHz | Wireless FC ↔ ground station link (MAVLink) |
| 6 | GPS, Holybro M9N | Positioning/navigation for autonomous & assisted modes |
| 7 | Transmitter | Sends pilot control commands |
| 8 | Receiver | Relays transmitter signal to flight controller |
| 9 | Battery, LiPo 5200mAh 35C (6S) | Power supply for entire system |
| 10 | Power module | Regulates/distributes battery power to FC and peripherals |
| 11 | Vibration damper | Isolates FC from frame vibration (protects IMU accuracy) |
| 12 | PDB (S500 frame) | Distributes power throughout the airframe |
| 13 | Arms & landing gear (x4 each) | Structural support, stability on takeoff/landing |
| 14 | Propellers, 1045 (x4) | Converts motor torque to thrust |

 Pixhawk 6C connections

 ESC (via I/O port)

| Pin | Function |
|---|---|
| Signal | To motor's signal pin (motor N → output pin N) |
| Ground | To GND pin |
| Power | Red wire disconnected/insulated on standard BEC ESCs — Pixhawk's dedicated power module handles this instead |

GPS (M9N, via GPS1 port)

| Wire | Signal | Function |
|---|---|---|
| Red | VCC_5V | Power supply |
| White | TX | Data out from Pixhawk |
| Yellow | RX | Data into Pixhawk |
| Green | I2C1_SCL | Compass clock |
| Blue | I2C1_SDA | Compass data |
| Orange | Safety | Safety switch |
| Purple | Safety LED | Safety LED |
| Brown | VCC_3V3 | 3.3V peripheral power |
| Grey | Buzzer | Piezo buzzer |
| Black | GND | Ground |

GPS must be mounted with its front aligned to the vehicle front for accurate heading.

 Telemetry (433 MHz, via TELEM1 port)

| Pin | Signal | Function |
|---|---|---|
| 1 (Red) | 5V | Power |
| 2 (Black) | UART7_TX (out) | FC TX → Radio RX |
| 3 (Black) | UART7_RX (in) | FC RX ← Radio TX |
| 4 (Black) | UART7_CTS (in) | Flow control |
| 5 (Black) | UART7_RTS (out) | Flow control |
| 6 (Black) | GND | Ground |

Power (via POWER1 port, from Power Module)

| Pin | Signal | Voltage |
|---|---|---|
| 1 (Red) | VCC_5V | +5V input (4.75–5.5V) |
| 2 (Black) | VCC_5V | +5V input, parallel (current capacity) |
| 3 (Black) | CURRENT | Analog — battery current draw |
| 4 (Black) | VOLTAGE | Analog — battery voltage |
| 5 (Black) | GND | Ground |
| 6 (Black) | GND | Ground |

Sizing math

Weight budget (example build):

| Component | Weight |
|---|---|
| Frame | 500 g |
| 4 motors | 220 g |
| 4 ESCs | 120 g |
| Pixhawk 6C | 40 g |
| GPS | 25 g |
| Telemetry | 30 g |
| Battery | 600 g |
| Other (mounts, damper, etc.) | 150 g |
|Total| ≈1685 g (1.7 kg)|

Thrust requirement (2:1 thrust-to-weight ratio):
- Total thrust needed = 2 × 1.7 kg = 3.4 kg
- Per motor (4 motors) = 850 g

Battery max continuous current: Capacity (Ah) × C-rating → 5.2 Ah × 35C = 182 A

Estimated flight time: Capacity ÷ average current draw → 5.2 Ah ÷ 20 A ≈ 15.6 minutes (varies with payload, maneuvering, wind, battery health)

ESC sizing rule: ESC rating must exceed max motor current. Here, 18 A motor draw → 40 A ESC selected (safe margin).

